# TASK 3: Implement Citizen Ward Membership Verification

After successful Citizen authentication, redirect the user to the Citizen Portal.

However, authentication and ward membership are two different processes.

A successfully registered Citizen is not automatically a member of any ward community.

Implement the following workflow.

## 3.1 Citizen Authentication

After successful registration or login:

- Create or authenticate the Citizen account.
- Redirect the Citizen to the Citizen Portal.
- Allow the Citizen to access the general portal.
- Check whether the Citizen has already submitted a ward membership request.
- Check whether the request is pending, approved, or rejected.

Do not automatically assign ward membership during registration.

## 3.2 Ward Community Membership Request

Inside the Citizen Portal, provide a section for joining the appropriate Ward Community.

Display a form requesting the necessary residential and contact information.

Required fields:

- Full Name (prepopulate from the registered account where possible)
- Phone Number
- Residential Address
- District
- Ward Number

Validate all required information before submission.

The Citizen must select their actual residential ward.

## 3.3 Membership Request Submission

When the Citizen submits the form:

1. Send the request to the backend.
2. Save the request in the database.
3. Associate it with the authenticated Citizen ID.
4. Set the initial membership status to Pending.
5. Make the request available in the System Administrator portal for verification.

Do not automatically add the Citizen to a ward group after form submission.

## 3.4 System Administrator Verification

The System Administrator must have the ability to:

- View pending ward membership requests.
- View the Citizen's submitted information.
- Verify the residential address and ward information.
- Approve the request.
- Reject the request.
- Provide a rejection reason when necessary.

When approved:

- Update the membership status to Approved.
- Associate the Citizen with the verified ward.
- Add the Citizen to the corresponding ward community.
- Enable access to the relevant ward-specific features.

When rejected:

- Keep the Citizen outside the ward community.
- Display the rejection status and reason.
- Allow the Citizen to correct the information and submit another request where appropriate.

Prevent duplicate active membership requests and conflicting ward memberships.

## 3.5 Ward Group Access Restrictions

Ward membership must be enforced throughout the application.

A Citizen who has not received approval must not be treated as a member of any ward group.

Implement the following restrictions:

| Feature | Before Ward Approval | After Ward Approval |
|---|---|---|
| Citizen Portal | Accessible | Accessible |
| Personal Profile | Accessible | Accessible |
| Ward Community | Restricted | Accessible |
| Ward Announcements | Restricted | Accessible |
| Ward Notifications | Restricted | Accessible |
| Ward Discussions | Restricted | Accessible |
| Community Support | Restricted | Accessible |
| Ward-specific information | Restricted | Accessible according to permissions |

Important:

- Pending Citizens must not receive ward-specific announcements or notifications.
- Rejected Citizens must not receive ward-specific announcements or notifications.
- Only approved members of Ward 43 should receive Ward 43 community information.
- Ward 43 members must not receive Ward 44 or Ward 45 private community information.
- Apply the same restriction to all wards.

Implement these checks on both frontend and backend.

Do not rely only on hiding menu items. Unauthorized API requests must also be rejected.

## 3.6 Membership Status UI

Display the appropriate membership status in the Citizen Portal.

Possible statuses:

- Not Submitted
- Pending Verification
- Approved – Ward Member
- Rejected

Show a suitable message based on the current status.

For example:

Pending:
"Your ward membership request has been submitted and is awaiting verification by the System Administrator."

Approved:
"Your ward membership has been approved. You can now access your Ward Community."

Rejected:
"Your ward membership request was rejected. Please review the reason and update your information."

Do not display unnecessary ward-specific notifications to users who are not approved members.

